WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.267 --> 00:00:02.902
-Welcome back to "Late Night,"
everyone.

00:00:02.902 --> 00:00:06.606
My next guest is a Democratic
Senator from New Mexico.

00:00:06.606 --> 00:00:07.940
His new book,

00:00:07.940 --> 00:00:10.577
"The Way Forward: Meeting
the Challenges of a New America"

00:00:10.577 --> 00:00:11.944
is on shelves now.

00:00:11.944 --> 00:00:14.881
Please welcome to the show,
Senator David Jimenez.

00:00:14.881 --> 00:00:21.053
[ Cheers and applause ]
♪♪

00:00:21.053 --> 00:00:26.292
♪♪

00:00:26.292 --> 00:00:28.861
So great to have you here today.
-Thank you for having me, sir.

00:00:28.861 --> 00:00:30.863
-So I have a lot
to talk to you about.

00:00:30.863 --> 00:00:33.466
But before that, I heard
that you might actually have

00:00:33.466 --> 00:00:35.735
something that you want to make
an announcement about.

00:00:35.735 --> 00:00:37.069
-That's right, Seth.

00:00:37.069 --> 00:00:38.604
I would like to
formally announce

00:00:38.604 --> 00:00:41.441
that I am running for President
of the United States.

00:00:41.441 --> 00:00:44.744
-Well, that is very exciting.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:44.744 --> 00:00:47.713
Very, very exciting.
-Thank you.

00:00:47.713 --> 00:00:48.981
It is exciting.

00:00:48.981 --> 00:00:53.952
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:53.952 --> 00:00:55.822
It is exciting stuff.

00:00:55.822 --> 00:00:58.891
You know, we have some real
challenges to face in America.

00:00:58.891 --> 00:01:00.560
Some of our most dire ones yet.

00:01:00.560 --> 00:01:02.761
And I believe
I have the solutions.

00:01:02.761 --> 00:01:04.864
-That's amazing,
Senator Jimenez.

00:01:04.864 --> 00:01:07.166
And now that you're entering
what is a very --

00:01:07.166 --> 00:01:09.302
let's be honest, a very crowded
Democratic field,

00:01:09.302 --> 00:01:11.904
can you explain why
you've chosen to run now?

00:01:11.904 --> 00:01:15.975
-Seth, the American people need
someone to fight for them

00:01:15.975 --> 00:01:19.545
based on their interests,
and lead them to a new day.

00:01:19.545 --> 00:01:21.247
-And I'm sorry -- who are you?

00:01:21.247 --> 00:01:23.449
-I'm Senator Christine Packard,

00:01:23.449 --> 00:01:26.619
and I'm running for President
of the United States.

00:01:26.619 --> 00:01:28.621
[ Cheers and applause ]
You can --

00:01:28.621 --> 00:01:32.659
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:35.461 --> 00:01:37.596
You can read about it
in my new book,

00:01:37.596 --> 00:01:39.732
"Fighting for a New Day:

00:01:39.732 --> 00:01:43.302
Fighting the Good Fight
for a Good America."

00:01:43.302 --> 00:01:45.504
-Oh, okay. Well --
This is a little awkward.

00:01:45.504 --> 00:01:47.072
This doesn't really
work that well

00:01:47.072 --> 00:01:48.741
if there are two people
at the --

00:01:48.741 --> 00:01:51.778
-Seth, I'm sorry,
but we need to usher in

00:01:51.778 --> 00:01:54.880
a new America
with what I am calling

00:01:54.880 --> 00:01:56.849
a "New American Century,"

00:01:56.849 --> 00:02:00.586
filled with promise for
a new century for Americans.

00:02:00.586 --> 00:02:03.856
This is why I'm running for
President of the United States.

00:02:03.856 --> 00:02:05.124
-Uh-huh.

00:02:05.124 --> 00:02:10.997
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:10.997 --> 00:02:12.932
-You can read it in my book,

00:02:12.932 --> 00:02:16.936
"A New Century: Making a New
America for a New Century."

00:02:16.936 --> 00:02:18.303
[ Laughter ]

00:02:18.303 --> 00:02:20.373
-I got to say, it was already
such a crowded field,

00:02:20.373 --> 00:02:22.008
and now there are
so many people running,

00:02:22.008 --> 00:02:23.976
I'm having trouble
keeping track of everyone.

00:02:23.976 --> 00:02:26.612
Is anyone else running?
-We are.

00:02:26.612 --> 00:02:27.947
-Oh.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:27.947 --> 00:02:29.649
Well, like, just
in interest of time,

00:02:29.649 --> 00:02:32.118
could you guys explain
your platforms together?

00:02:32.118 --> 00:02:33.586
-Seth, I am the...

00:02:33.586 --> 00:02:35.154
-Father of three wonderful...
-Mother of two beautiful...

00:02:35.154 --> 00:02:36.655
-...children, and I believe...

00:02:36.655 --> 00:02:37.857
-the future
is worth fighting for.

00:02:37.857 --> 00:02:39.025
-It's worthwhile to fight for
the future.

00:02:39.025 --> 00:02:40.559
-Right now, we are more divided
than ever.

00:02:40.559 --> 00:02:41.995
-Our nation is more polarized
than ever.

00:02:41.995 --> 00:02:43.296
-...but I believe I have the
strength and the fortitude...

00:02:43.296 --> 00:02:44.664
-...courage and determination
to lead us...

00:02:44.664 --> 00:02:46.165
-...to take us...
-...forward, together.

00:02:46.165 --> 00:02:47.433
This is why I'm running

00:02:47.433 --> 00:02:49.869
for President of the
United States of America.

00:02:49.869 --> 00:02:56.576
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:56.576 --> 00:02:58.978
-You can read about it
in my new book...

00:02:58.978 --> 00:03:00.613
-"Becoming the Future..."
"Changing the Present..."

00:03:00.613 --> 00:03:02.281
-"How to Change the Present..."
-"How to Alter the Past..."

00:03:02.281 --> 00:03:04.149
-"...And Abandon the Past."
-"...And Become the Future."

00:03:04.149 --> 00:03:05.984
[ Laughter and cheering ]

00:03:05.984 --> 00:03:09.789
-All right, you know,
there are a lot of you.

00:03:09.789 --> 00:03:11.857
I'm having trouble keeping you
all straight.

00:03:11.857 --> 00:03:13.559
Ultimately it's up to
the voters to decide,

00:03:13.559 --> 00:03:15.561
so maybe it would be a good idea
to turn it over to the audience

00:03:15.561 --> 00:03:17.096
for a question -- anyone?

00:03:17.096 --> 00:03:19.798
-I have a question, Seth.
-Yes, go ahead.

00:03:19.798 --> 00:03:23.536
-Seth, America
is at a crossroads.

00:03:23.536 --> 00:03:25.972
We have to decide whether
we want to go forwards

00:03:25.972 --> 00:03:28.374
into the future or backward
into the past.

00:03:28.374 --> 00:03:30.043
[ Laughter ]

00:03:30.043 --> 00:03:33.046
I believe I am the one
to lead us forward.

00:03:33.046 --> 00:03:35.081
[ Laughter ]

00:03:35.081 --> 00:03:40.086
This is why I'm running for
President of the United States!

00:03:40.086 --> 00:03:46.059
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:51.129 --> 00:03:57.070
Read about it in my new book,
"Choosing the Future:

00:03:57.070 --> 00:04:01.040
How to Abandon America's Past
and Move Forward to its Future."

00:04:01.040 --> 00:04:03.142
[ Laughter ]
-Oh, man, there's...

00:04:03.142 --> 00:04:07.980
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:07.980 --> 00:04:10.515
There's some more people here
with some more books,

00:04:10.515 --> 00:04:13.419
I just noticed, so, uh...

00:04:13.419 --> 00:04:16.055
No offense, but I really don't
want to hear another person

00:04:16.055 --> 00:04:17.957
say they're
running for president.

00:04:17.957 --> 00:04:21.627
-I'm running for president!
-Oh, man.

00:04:21.627 --> 00:04:25.330
-I think there is no way with --

00:04:25.330 --> 00:04:27.933
there is no one with the
experience that I have to bring

00:04:27.933 --> 00:04:29.368
to the White House.

00:04:29.368 --> 00:04:31.737
That is why, until --

00:04:31.737 --> 00:04:33.739
with the two remaining years
before I die...

00:04:33.739 --> 00:04:35.741
-Oh, boy.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:35.741 --> 00:04:39.211
-...I am running for President
of the United States!

00:04:39.211 --> 00:04:40.980
Read about it in my book!

00:04:40.980 --> 00:04:42.982
[ Laughter ]

00:04:42.982 --> 00:04:48.354
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:48.354 --> 00:04:50.123
"I'm Old."
-"I'm Old."

00:04:50.123 --> 00:04:51.723
-"I'm Old."
-Your book --

00:04:51.723 --> 00:04:53.959
Your book is called
"I'm Old"?

00:04:53.959 --> 00:04:57.029
-I'm extremely old, Seth.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:57.029 --> 00:04:59.231
-All right. Look, I think
I'm going to end this.

00:04:59.231 --> 00:05:00.766
I don't know if we're
actually getting

00:05:00.766 --> 00:05:02.068
any new information here.

00:05:02.068 --> 00:05:03.902
-Seth, I'm running because
I believe in

00:05:03.902 --> 00:05:06.171
bipartisan solutions that work.

00:05:06.171 --> 00:05:08.474
-Work because America needs
a leader.

00:05:08.474 --> 00:05:11.510
-A leader who will put
middle-class Americans --

00:05:11.510 --> 00:05:14.213
-Americans ahead of
special interests.

00:05:14.213 --> 00:05:15.948
-You know what, that was
very good, you guys.

00:05:15.948 --> 00:05:19.085
I just think --
Oh, my goodness! Uh...

00:05:19.085 --> 00:05:20.486
Let me guess. You're --

00:05:20.486 --> 00:05:22.054
You're running
for president, too?

00:05:22.054 --> 00:05:26.092
-Seth, it is
with some regrets

00:05:26.092 --> 00:05:28.260
that I am announcing that I am

00:05:28.260 --> 00:05:31.697
suspending my campaign to be
President of the United States.

00:05:31.697 --> 00:05:34.400
-Oh, I didn't even know
you were running, but --

00:05:34.400 --> 00:05:38.437
-Words cannot express how
grateful I am to all of you,

00:05:38.437 --> 00:05:41.006
my true friends.
-Oh, I'm sorry, you're out, too?

00:05:41.006 --> 00:05:43.675
-My true friends who helped me
in this fight.

00:05:43.675 --> 00:05:46.679
-No! Not you, David Jimenez!
[ Laughter ]

00:05:46.679 --> 00:05:49.915
-It's clear that my past
was too difficult

00:05:49.915 --> 00:05:51.417
for us to overcome.

00:05:51.417 --> 00:05:54.686
-And the numbers just weren't
working our way.

00:05:54.686 --> 00:05:57.356
-While I believe in
what we fought for,

00:05:57.356 --> 00:06:00.026
I also believe I am too old.

00:06:00.026 --> 00:06:01.927
[ Laughter ]

00:06:01.927 --> 00:06:04.897
-The American people must make
a decision that represents

00:06:04.897 --> 00:06:07.166
our shared ideas.

00:06:07.166 --> 00:06:09.501
-Our shared ideals
of leading America

00:06:09.501 --> 00:06:12.571
to a brand-new future
and away from our past.

00:06:12.571 --> 00:06:14.640
-You can read about it
in my new book,

00:06:14.640 --> 00:06:18.110
"Clearing the Path:
Abandoning My Past

00:06:18.110 --> 00:06:21.013
as a Candidate for America's
Future as a Country."

00:06:21.013 --> 00:06:24.516
-Okay, I'm sorry. I am
just having a difficult time

00:06:24.516 --> 00:06:27.052
keeping straight which one
of you has dropped out so far.

00:06:27.052 --> 00:06:29.822
So, quick head count. Who is
still running for president?

00:06:29.822 --> 00:06:35.694
[ Laughter ]

00:06:35.694 --> 00:06:38.798
Does anyone want --
Does anyone --

00:06:38.798 --> 00:06:45.971
[ Applause ]

00:06:45.971 --> 00:06:48.874
Anyone interested
in vice president?

00:06:48.874 --> 00:06:50.409
-[Bleep] no.
-All right.

00:06:50.409 --> 00:06:52.578
[ Laughter ]
-Watch the language.

00:06:52.578 --> 00:06:54.513
You are very old!
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:54.513 --> 00:06:56.482
The 2020 Democratic candidates,
everyone.

00:06:56.482 --> 00:06:58.084
We'll be right back with more
"Late Night."

